			<div class="content" id="post-content-3911285">
									

<p>Dang this packs a good hard punch in not a lot of words, nice. Just wanted to clarify a few things though:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Once the target is incapacitated, often in contrast to their vocalizations of protest</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is the &quot;their&quot; the target or SCP-3544-B? From the log I assume it's the latter but it wasn't too clear for me on the first read through.</p>
<p>Also to add on to what Modern_Erasmus said above, I too thought the SCP had moved the heart because I thought the diagnosis was a post-event Foundation one. Maybe a wording like &quot;Further investigation into POI-3544-01's medical history revealed that she had previously been diagnosed with dextrocardia, a condition where the heart is on the right side of the chest.&quot; would be clearer?</p>

							</div>

								
					
