			<div class="content" id="post-content-3911439">
									

<p>Both valid points. I was a little worried myself that the former of those was confusing, but nobody else had pointed it out so I didn't worry that much. I like your rewording to emphasise medical <em>history</em> so I'll definitely include that, but I might add some dialogue to make it explicit that's why she survived.</p>
<p>I'm also glad you mentioned the &quot;not a lot of words&quot; - maybe it's been from a long history of clinical writing IRL, but even in fiction I like to convey as much as possible in as little as possible.</p>

